      "gate_id": "VAL-002",
      "notes": "The pivot gate COMPUTES ITS OWN EXPECTATION FROM THE COMMITTED IMAGE. The fixture decodes each PNG from disk and measures the alpha bounding box from its pixels; it never reads alpha_bounds_px from the catalog, because a check whose expectation comes from the artifact it checks agrees with itself whatever the asset does. Only pivot_rule is read from PropCatalog.json, and a missing or unrecognised rule FAILS rather than defaulting to a branch. lie_within takes the vertical centre of the box, ground_line its bottom row; pivot x is 0.5 in both, alignment Custom, tolerance one pixel. FOUND BY THIS FIXTURE, NOT AROUND IT: the first run failed because the ground-line expression was integer arithmetic and 16/188 evaluated to 0 -- the fixture disagreed with a correctly imported asset and said so, which is the behaviour the gate exists to produce.",
